# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# The ONLY secret this app has. Without it the assistant runs in offline mode:
# it still answers, from scripted responses assembled out of bundle.json, and
# labels every one of them as scripted. Nothing crashes and no page breaks.
#
# Get a key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# NEVER rename this to NEXT_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY. Next.js inlines any
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable into the JavaScript it sends to the browser, which on a
# public URL means publishing the key. It is read server-side only, in
# src/lib/chatHandler.ts, which only the /api/chat route imports.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL. Forces a model to the head of the selection queue.
#
# You should not normally need this. The server calls ListModels once per
# instance and picks the first model this key's project actually reports, from
# the preference order gemini-3.6-flash -> gemini-3.5-flash-lite ->
# gemini-2.5-flash, falling through on a 404. Set this only when you know a
# specific name works for your key — for example a tuned model that ListModels
# does not advertise. A name set here is tried FIRST and tried EVEN IF
# ListModels does not report it; if it fails, the rest of the chain still
# answers, so a typo here degrades rather than breaks.
#
# Server-side only. Never rename this to NEXT_PUBLIC_GEMINI_MODEL.
# GEMINI_MODEL=

# OPTIONAL. Pins which ENDPOINT the assistant uses.
#
#   interactions      POST /v1beta/interactions        (default, tried first)
#   generateContent   POST /v1beta/models/{m}:generateContent  (legacy fallback)
#
# You should not normally need this either. The server tries the Interactions
# API first and falls through to the legacy generateContent path automatically
# if the endpoint itself rejects the call, caching whichever one works for the
# life of the instance.
#
# It exists because which endpoint a key may use appears to depend on how the
# key was minted: new-style AI Studio auth keys (prefix "AQ.", now the default)
# are accepted by Interactions and appear to be refused by the legacy models/*
# paths, while older "AIza..." keys work on both. If you have watched one
# endpoint work for your key, pinning it here saves one round-trip per cold
# instance. An unrecognised value is ignored rather than fatal.
#
# Server-side only. Never rename this to NEXT_PUBLIC_GEMINI_TRANSPORT.
# GEMINI_TRANSPORT=
